 ## Background
-The Semantic Consistency Loss based on CLIP-ViT was introduced by DietNeRF in June 2021 [S1]. DietNeRF [51] proposed using CLIP-ViT [123] to extract image features and enforce semantic consistency in addition to standard photometric loss. The method was benchmarked on a subsampled NeRF synthetic dataset [1] and the DTU dataset [29]. The concept of using CLIP for semantic consistency in NeRFs was further explored in works like 360FusionNeRF [S3] and Blended-NeRF [S2], which adapted the loss for panoramic scenes and text-guided editing, respectively. Region Semantic Ranking Regularization [S4] later addressed the limitations of vanilla CLIP relevancy maps by incorporating SAM [31].
+The Semantic Consistency Loss based on CLIP-ViT was introduced by DietNeRF in June 2021 [S1]. DietNeRF proposed using CLIP-ViT to extract image features and enforce semantic consistency in addition to standard photometric loss [S1]. The method was benchmarked on a subsampled NeRF synthetic dataset and the DTU dataset [S1]. The concept of using CLIP for semantic consistency in NeRFs was further explored in works like 360FusionNeRF [S3] and Blended-NeRF [S2], which adapted the loss for panoramic scenes and text-guided editing, respectively. Region Semantic Ranking Regularization [S4] later addressed the limitations of vanilla CLIP relevancy maps by incorporating SAM [S4].
 
